omx-clap-host (0.11.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.11.0
  * abi: record the baseline of 0.11.0 with make abi-baseline
  * abi: the MPE zones are ABI 9, appended after the voice info of ABI 8
    (#139, #91)
  * stage: the zones struct comment names omx_clap_mpe_take (#139)
  * stage: document the MPE master bits for make docs (#139)
  * Version 0.11.0: two MPE zones add to the ABI (#139)
  * stage: a lower and an upper MPE zone held together; a master reaches its
    own zone's notes (#139)
  * lv2_run_test: hold the worker inside work() instead of racing its poll
    (#101, #113)
  * tests: jack_transport_e2e refuses the probe's -1 reading as zero drift
    (#147)
  * doc: two MPE zones held together, master expressions reach their own zone
    (#139)
  * ci: build plugin-hostd's RPMs without its check stage (#166)
  * Version 0.11.0: omx_clap_host_voice_info is an addition to the ABI (#91)
  * core: read clap.voice-info at activate, answer it with
    omx_clap_host_voice_info; ABI 8 (#91)
  * doc: an instrument's voice info, read at activate (#91)
  * tests: jack_transport_e2e reads beats against seconds in one process()
    (#147)
  * tests: dialect_doc_check.sh compares reference.md with clap_stage.h on
    the passed message types (#93)
  * docs: note dialect rules and the plugin window say what the code does
    (#93)
  * param_contract_test: pin OMX_CLAP_PARAM_SCALES ordinals and count to
    omx-contract's PARAM_SCALES (#153)
  * lv2 core: free the side-chain names of a refused open (#54)
  * test-contract: hold each hosting limit and refusal code to what
    omx-contract's reader reads, one sabotage arm per value (#146)
  * BUILDING: the hosting headers are held value by value to the reader's
    values (#146)
  * bench-stage: copy omx_clap_midi.h beside the relaxed clap_stage.h; run it
    in CI (#165)
  * ci: build plugin-hostd's DEBs with nocheck (#166, #142)
  * omx-contract floor 2.16.0, where OMX_ORACLE_FULL_RATES_* first exists
    (#150)
  * tests: take the oracle rates from OMX_ORACLE_FULL_RATES_INIT (#150)
  * omx-clap-host: a note verb with no room in the queue answers -517 (#122)
  * omx-clap-host: answer plugin-hostd's note verbs on the command socket
    (#122)
  * Build against plugin-hostd 0.4.0, whose header declares the note verbs
    (#122)
  * abi: check the layout of every public structure with pahole, atomics
    included (#117)
  * stage: the published transport may have an audio thread as its writer
    (#121)
  * lv2: admit an instrument, a MIDI input and audio outputs with no audio
    input (#132)
  * ci: run make test-socket against the protocol library CI builds (#103)
  * stage: a late NOTE_END frees an id only while it names the event's note
    (#138)
  * doc: the gesture ends after a drop and the R3 check after a rescan (#141)
  * param contract: check R3 after each params.rescan (#141)
  * omx-clap-host: end the open gestures when the parameter ring dropped
    events (#141)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:37:31 +0000
